staggered constrained transport.

Stress-energy divergence ($\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu}=0$), Liouville phase-volume
conservation ($df/dt=0$), and symplectic 2-form integrity are continuously monitored by
a hardware feedback bus that autonomously triggers mesh re-clustering and subcycling
when invariants drift. Execution states are encapsulated via ML-KEM-1024, evaluated
over homomorphic CKKS SIMD ciphertexts, and recursively proven via Halo2/Plonky3
arithmetization over $2^{20}$ constraint rows. Epoch states are committed to an
immutable BLAKE3 Merkle ledger. UAS-CPE resolves relativistic blast waves, Kerr
magnetospheres, and self-gravitating core collapses while producing succinct,
mathematically verifiable proofs of physical and computational validity.
\end{abstract}

